@* Ported from Index.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs - the Inventory module landing
   region.

   CONTENT-FREE BY ORIGIN, and that is a verified fact rather than an omission: the .ascx
   contained ONLY the license comment and the <%@ Control %> directive, the designer file
   declared no fields, and OnControlLoad's body was empty. The legacy screen rendered an
   empty region; emitting markup here would ADD a screen the module never had. Its entire
   server-side behaviour is what MixERPUserControl runs for every control - the
   Log.Verbose("{Control} initialized.") entry plus CheckAccessLevel and
   CheckTransactionPostingStatus.

   The original declared no OverridePath, AccessLevel, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme or
   IsLandingPage override and implemented no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control declares
    ///     it. The legacy body was ALREADY empty (see the note above), so an empty body here
    ///     is the faithful port, not a stub.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }
}
